# Rule Sets Configuration

## Shared Filter

Shared scope filter (applies to all four rule sets)

| Item | Setting |
| --- | --- |
| Book category | Exclude non-standard, non-trading books |
| Book-name keywords | Exclude books whose name contains the agreed keywords (e.g. watch books belonging to another desk) |
| Bloomberg | Taken out of scope |
| X-Force | Put back at the end of the call so exceptions still show. Including it moves the count from 490 to 778 |
| Net effect | Scope is about 4,000 books smaller than before (transcript is garbled on the baseline) |
| Source: call transcript. All four rule sets use this same overall filter. |  |

## 1 SA-BAU

Rule set 1: SA-BAU (generic basic set)

| Rule | Condition (filter) | Expectation | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Trading book must be SA contributory | Trading book (pure trading, not IRT/ART). Exclude CVA = yes (removes the SA=no / CVA=yes population) | SA = yes | Keep expectation 1 only; drop old expectations 2-4. SA-only, does not referee between SA and CVA. |
| Remaining pre-combined basic rules | Same shared filter | Unchanged | Take out of the current run and re-fence here. |
| Presentation | n/a | n/a | Run first for the department head this afternoon: 'this is what goes to audit'. |
| Open point | Possible second expectation to flag yes/yes books | Not settled | May stay here or move to the cross SA-CVA set. |

## 2 CVA

Rule set 2: CVA (pure SA-CVA / XVA)

| Rule | Condition (filter) | Expectation | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| CVA basic rules | CVA/XVA books only; ignore the SA flag | Book follows its own basic CVA logic | Fenced from SA. Not in scope of the audit yet. No specific rule IDs named in the transcript. |
| XVA-desk-specific checks | XVA desk books | Not specified | Suggested: a separate rule block per desk (XVA, later equity or prime finance) so special treatment does not pollute the general rules. |
| Known cleanup | Empty books and exposure books | n/a | Already cleaned up per ul0794. |
| Run timing | n/a | n/a | Run after the call. |

## 3 Cross SA-CVA

Rule set 3: Cross SA-CVA (SA vs SA-CVA tracking)

| Rule | Condition (filter) | Expectation | Notes | Count |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| No coexistence across frameworks | Trading book | Not yes in both SA and SA-CVA | Currently 1 book yes/yes | 1 |
| Trading book flagged no in both | Trading book, SA = no and CVA = no | Not both no | Mostly equity dual-booking books. Do not show or commit to fixing by year-end. | 489 |
| Blank or null flags | SA or CVA empty/null | Flag any | Confirmed none exist | 0 |
| Not an exception | SA = no, CVA = yes | Valid | Legitimate CVA-eligible books; excluded from the check |  |
| Total exceptions (about 500) |  |  | Sum of the counts above is 490; transcript quotes roughly 500 | 490 |
| Do not show this set to the department head this afternoon. Use later as management insight to ask for resources. |  |  |  |  |

## 4 Analytics

Rule set 4: Analytics (overarching, framework-agnostic)

| Rule | Condition (filter) | Expectation | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| At least one BAU flag populated | FO or Traded Risk MO book, not non-standard/non-trading. Ideally only PnL-generating books, trading or banking | At least one of the four BAU flags = yes (not all blank or no) | Source: PRA finding. Department head asked HMS for a preemptive rule; this is an internal check ahead of that. Expect many exceptions (unused books). |
| Anchor flag | Not decided | n/a | Unsure whether to anchor on book category or the PnL flag (field name unclear in transcript). |
| HMS follow-up | n/a | HMS defaults the BAU flags to yes at booking | Action item for HMS, alongside the internal check. |
| Presentation | n/a | n/a | Show as a separate, later item, not in the first presentation. |

